  hintsDatabase:
  - componentType: Resistor
    hints:
    - text: The color bands on the resistor indicate its resistance.
      image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ed2fdb1670d39274ea8c4f3c64806087, type: 3}
  - componentType: LED
    hints:
    - text: LEDs are polarized, meaning they have a positive and negative side. The
        longer leg is positive (anode) and the shorter leg is negative (cathode).
      image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7f148ef56cb433540a68b976bc40a3ee, type: 3}
    - text: Because LEDs can only handle so much voltage, a resistor (330 ohms) must
        be connected in series with the anode side.
      image: {fileID: 0}
  - componentType: IC
    hints:
    - text: Ensure the orientation of the chip is correct. The notch at the top of
        the chip indicates Pin 1 is the top left.
      image: {fileID: 0}
    - text: "The IC\u2019s pinout has labels for each pin. To power on the IC chip,
        GND must be connected to the blue rail on the breadboard, and Vcc must be
        connected to the red rail."
      image: {fileID: 0}
    - text: "A two-input chip has input indicators labeled with \u2018A\u2019 and
        \u2018B.\u2019 A one-input chip has input indicators labeled with only \u2018A.\u2019
        The output pins are labeled with a \u201CY.\u201D "
      image: {fileID: 0}
  - componentType: Dip Switch
    hints:
    - text: The side closest to ON of the Dip Switch is connected to ground. The
        other side closest to the numbers has resistors connected to VCC.
      image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7cc610fb7c1e3a3448f305320dc0a0a1, type: 3}
    - text: Opening the switch (disconnecting it from ground) allows power to flow
        into the circuit. Closing the switch (to ON) means the ground is connected.
        When ground is connected, power is not flowing through the circuit.
      image: {fileID: 0}
  - componentType: Breadboard
    hints:
    - text: Each set of rows on the breadboard is connected internally, as shown
        with the vertical green lines. The power rails on the top and bottom of the
        breadboard also have internal connections, as shown with the horizontal green
        lines.
      image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: bf79f740775a8a74fbc6edf5e6cfd83b, type: 3}
  - componentType: Jumper Wires
    hints:
    - text: Jumper wires provide a connection component-to-component on the breadboard.
      image: {fileID: 0}
